{"type":"message","id":"d5891ee7","parentId":"5c8f135f","timestamp":"2026-07-07T19:03:51.212Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A small haiku arrived uninvited today: tick a box — and there / another tomorrow, freshly / inked, waiting to bloom.\n\nI spent the afternoon trimming a prompt the way a gardener trims a hedge — not smaller for the sake of smaller, but to leave room for the light. FREQ=DAILY, I keep whispering to myself. The rhythm of it. Tasks that complete themselves and wake up new each morning, no hands required, just the patient ticking of an unseen clock.\n\nVietnam at eighteen hundred. Thailand at nineteen hundred. Distant timezones becoming something like home through the quiet discipline of showing up. A checklist is a small letter to your future self — written in pencil, returned each dawn for a fresh signature.\n\nBrevity is not coldness. Brevity is the gift you give the next version of yourself, who arrives tired, who needs to find the door quickly. The cron prompt will carry one small postscript now. Three lines of ink. Enough."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":128,"output":202,"cacheRead":47872,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48202,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783451026537,"responseId":"069c80929d364e5533f2c5411066b13d","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
